@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
title Behavior - Capture a populated backup
actor "Release operator" as actor
box "Release tooling - backend/src/MissionControl.Operations" #E0F2FE
  participant "OperationsConsole" as console
  participant "CaptureBackupOperation" as capture
end box
box "Selected SQL provider" #FFF4E5
  database "Source SQL\n(read-only during capture)" as source
end box
box "Backup storage - facility <TO SUPPLY>" #F2F4F7
  collections "Backup storage" as storage
end box
box "Release records - docs/operations" #ECFDF3
  participant "RecoveryRecord" as record
end box
actor -> console : backup (source write freeze recorded in runbook)
console -> capture : Run with bound RecoveryOptions
break Source, storage, or external credentials not configured
  capture --> console : Refused before any provider command
  console -> record : Outcome Failed: configuration incomplete
  console --> actor : Exit non-zero; nothing ran against the source
end
capture -> source : Read DataFingerprint in one read-only transaction
source --> capture : Counts and ordered digests: IDs; account roles / active flags; lead categories;\nparent / responsible-lead / assignee links; sibling / backlog positions; board placements;\nsprint membership / initial scope / scope changes; closure snapshots; samples
capture -> source : L2-044 provider backup command <TO SUPPLY> (reads only)
source -> storage : Write backup artifact
break Backup command fails or storage access is denied
  storage --> capture : Provider error
  capture --> console : Failed step; provider message without secrets
  console -> record : Outcome Failed; no backup point recorded
  console --> actor : Failure and access guidance; source unchanged
end
capture -> storage : Provider read-only verification; SHA-256 checksum
break Artifact unreadable or incomplete
  storage --> capture : Verification error
  capture --> console : Failed: artifact not usable for restore
  console -> record : Outcome Failed; artifact marked unusable
  console --> actor : Capture again; no backup point claimed
end
storage --> capture : Verified artifact and checksum
capture --> console : Backup point, artifact location, checksum, fingerprint
console -> record : L2-044.3 start/end, backup point, checksum, fingerprint; Outcome Captured
console --> actor : Record path for the restore rehearsal
note over console, storage
No API call and no write reaches the source:
a sign-in would append an audit event to it.
end note
@enduml
